# Everything in this folder is copied onto Linux machines, usually from a Windows checkout, so
# it must keep LF endings whatever the checkout's own setting is.
#
# Patterns here are relative to THIS folder. Until 29 Sep 2026 they were written with the full
# path (scripts/linked-helper/*.py), which matches nothing from inside the folder - so the .py
# files were checked out CRLF on Windows and copied to machines that way. Python reads a CRLF
# file happily, which is why nobody noticed; a script run by its own first line would not start.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
